From aeeee912a9902ffd80a05befc627aa0f42c6005f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Feb 2026 09:45:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] fix: Add sortOrder to WMOAreaTable meta matching stock
 Blizzard format (I-128, I-129)

The 3.3.5a client expects WMOAreaTable.dbc records sorted by
(wmo_id, name_set_id, wmo_group_id), not by id. Without sortOrder,
DBCTool exported records in MySQL primary key order, breaking client
WMO area detection in Ironforge, Exodar, and other WMO-interior zones.

Closes I-128, Closes I-129

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 meta/wmoareatable.meta.json | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/meta/wmoareatable.meta.json b/meta/wmoareatable.meta.json
index 46835ac..cbb1aa6 100644
--- a/meta/wmoareatable.meta.json
+++ b/meta/wmoareatable.meta.json
@@ -3,6 +3,20 @@
   "primaryKeys": [
     "id"
   ],
+  "sortOrder": [
+    {
+      "name": "wmo_id",
+      "direction": "ASC"
+    },
+    {
+      "name": "name_set_id",
+      "direction": "ASC"
+    },
+    {
+      "name": "wmo_group_id",
+      "direction": "ASC"
+    }
+  ],
   "fields": [
     {
       "name": "id",
-- 
