From 9c5a7390facc9ddccd376cdf0dd5e5ab710c21d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 03:13:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat: Zeppelin DBCTool customizations - column defaults,
 extra metas, 3.3.5 bindings (F-206)

- src/db_import.go: createTable emits DEFAULT 0 on every numeric column (INT,
  INT UNSIGNED, TINYINT UNSIGNED, DECIMAL, and the trailing Loc flags column) so
  partial INSERT SET statements in zpak dbc/*.sql do not need to name every field.
- meta/: add glyphproperties and the four objecteffect* table definitions.
- original_bindings_335/: 98 stock 3.3.5 column binding dumps. These are a live
  dependency of Zeppelin-Craft cli/lib/spell_editor_views.py (BINDINGS_DIR), which
  pairs each binding with its meta to build the spell_editor PascalCase views.
  Caveat: at least WorldStateUI.txt is wrong - see I-166. Cross-check the Noggit
  dbd before trusting one.
- .gitignore: spell_editor_views.sql is a stale generated artifact, superseded by
  the in-memory generator in Zeppelin-Craft.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
